What:		/sys/kernel/ashmem/
Date:		Feb 2025
Contact:	Alice Ryhl <aliceryhl@google.com>
Description:
		/sys/kernel/ashmem/ contains a single node that can be used
		to adjust different characteristics of the ashmem driver's
		behavior.

What:		/sys/kernel/ashmem/unpin
Date:		Feb 2025
Contact:	Alice Ryhl <aliceryhl@google.com>
Description:
		Determines the behavior of the ASHMEM_UNPIN ioctl.

		A value of "shrinker" indicates that unpinned pages should be
		freed by a shrinker if the system is under memory pressure.

		A value of "immediately" indicates that calls to ASHMEM_UNPIN
		should free the pages immediately.

		A value of "ignore" indicates that calls to ASHMEM_UNPIN should
		be ignored.

What:		/sys/kernel/ashmem/ignore_unset_prot_read
Date:		Feb 2025
Contact:	Alice Ryhl <aliceryhl@google.com>
Description:
		Determines whether the SET_PROT_MASK ioctl should ignore
		attempts to unset the PROT_READ bit.

		This is a boolean option. When the value is 1, calls to
		SET_PROT_MASK ignore the PROT_READ bit given by userspace.

What:		/sys/kernel/ashmem/ignore_unset_prot_exec
Date:		Feb 2025
Contact:	Alice Ryhl <aliceryhl@google.com>
Description:
		Determines whether the SET_PROT_MASK ioctl should ignore
		attempts to unset the PROT_EXEC bit.

		This is a boolean option. When the value is 1, calls to
		SET_PROT_MASK ignore the PROT_EXEC bit given by userspace.
